      "message": "`canAcceptDrop()` checks `this.disabled` on the drop target, but neither `?draggable`, `handleChipDragStart()`, nor `removeAccount()` checks `this.disabled` on the source list (`computeRemovable()` only checks `this.readonly`).\n\nIf a list is disabled (for example, while `\u003cgr-reply-dialog\u003e` is actively submitting and `this.disabled \u003d true`), chips inside it can still be dragged out and removed into another list.\n\nCould we add `!this.disabled` to the chip\u0027s draggable condition (and in `handleChipDragStart` / `removeAccount`)?\n\n```diff\n@@ -194,5 +194,6 @@\n               ?removable\u003d${this.computeRemovable(account)}\n               ?draggable\u003d${this.chipDraggable \u0026\u0026\n+              !this.disabled \u0026\u0026\n               isAccount(account) \u0026\u0026\n               this.computeRemovable(account)}\n```",
