      "side": 1,
      "message": "If a user cancels a drag while hovering over a target list (e.g. by pressing Escape, dragging outside the browser window, or dropping onto an unhandled area), the HTML5 drag-and-drop specification dictates that `dragend` fires on the dragged chip, but neither `dragleave` nor `drop` fires on the hovered target element.\n\nBecause `handleChipDragEnd()` only nulls `activeChipDrag`, the hovered `\u003cgr-account-list\u003e` will remain stuck with the `.drag-over` class (showing the dashed outline and background highlight) indefinitely.\n\nCould we clean up any active `.drag-over` classes on drag end? For example:\n\n```ts\n  private handleChipDragEnd() {\n    activeChipDrag \u003d null;\n    document\n      .querySelectorAll(\u0027gr-account-list.drag-over\u0027)\n      .forEach(el \u003d\u003e el.classList.remove(\u0027drag-over\u0027));\n  }\n```",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "ce0d69a1ba815ab012d83d235deb6fbf3f8581ad",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
